## Serial GitLab agent loop

This project uses GitLab-only polling for one opted-in issue at a time. Set
`GITLAB_HOST` and numeric `GITLAB_PROJECT_ID`; the loop addresses that numeric
project instead of inferring it from `origin`. A Developer account can poll
eligible issues, so no webhook or inbound service is required:

```bash
agent-work run-next --json
agent-work run-next --apply --json
```

An applied run uses a dedicated agent checkout, opens one MR, and
stops at `awaiting_human`. It never approves or merges. Enable the supplied
user-systemd timer only after a human explicitly authorizes unattended
publication, the service identity is constrained, and a Maintainer has verified
independent approval safeguards (a Developer `403` is inconclusive). See
[`docs/how-to/setup-serial-gitlab-agent-loop.md`](docs/how-to/setup-serial-gitlab-agent-loop.md),
[`docs/reference/serial-gitlab-agent-loop.md`](docs/reference/serial-gitlab-agent-loop.md),
and [`.agents/skills/setup-agent-loop/SKILL.md`](.agents/skills/setup-agent-loop/SKILL.md).
